  "id": "morenada",
  "name": "Morenada (Bolivian brass-band fraternity dance)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Morenada is the dance of the morenos of the Bolivian altiplano and Puno, a central fraternity dance of the Carnaval de Oruro and La Paz's Gran Poder, whose dancers in heavy, ornate costumes whirl wooden matracas, ratchets that rattle over the music. It is played by bandas de bronce of trumpets, trombones, baritone horns and tubas over bass drum, snare and cymbals at a slow, heavy, swaying duple gait. The sousaphone card stands in for the bands' tubas.",
